---
// Blog post. Copy authored against briefs/maltipoo-daycare-options.json (2026-07-13).
// Evidence: positioning tie-in; zero breed-specific competition
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PawTrail from '../../components/PawTrail.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import AnswerCapsule from '../../components/AnswerCapsule.astro';
import FactsCard from '../../components/FactsCard.astro';
import FAQ from '../../components/FAQ.astro';
import CtaClose from '../../components/CtaClose.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
import { webPageSchema, breadcrumbSchema, faqSchema } from '../../lib/schema';
import featuredImg from '../../assets/site/34-maltipoo-grandma-sofa.webp';

const title = 'Daycare, Sitters and Helpers for Your Maltipoo | Maltipoo.sg';
const description =
  "When the flat empties out: honest options for a Maltipoo's daytime company in Singapore, from daycare and sitters to helper handovers and the split-shift trick.";

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Blog', url: '/blog' },
  { name: 'Daycare & Sitters', url: '/blog/maltipoo-daycare-options' },
];

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: "How much is dog daycare in Singapore?",
    a: "Typically tens of dollars per day with package discounts; rates vary by area and inclusions. The trial day tells you more than the price list.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can my helper legally walk the dog?",
    a: "Of course; the licence names an owner, not a walker. What matters is briefing, willingness and the before-9am heat rule.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is a camera and treat-dispenser enough?",
    a: "As monitoring, useful; as company, no. A camera shows you the loneliness in HD; it does not fix it.",
  },
  {
    q: "We both WFH but travel monthly. Workable?",
    a: "Very: that is a company-rich routine with occasional gaps, exactly what boarding, sitters or the free first-month boarding option are for. Plan the gaps before the trips.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can you leave a Maltipoo alone all day?",
    a: "No. A silent flat from 8am to 6pm every weekday is exactly what this attachment-dependent breed cannot do; it is the classic setup for separation anxiety. Build daytime company from daycare, a sitter, or a helper instead.",
  },
  {
    q: "How do I choose a good dog daycare?",
    a: "Vet it like a preschool: vaccination requirements actually enforced, toy dogs grouped away from the big-dog scrum, named staff ratios, and a trial half-day before you commit. Start with one or two days a week, not five.",
  },
];

const schemas = [
  webPageSchema({
    path: '/blog/maltipoo-daycare-options',
    title,
    description,
    aboutName: 'Maltipoo daytime care options',
    datePublished: '2026-07-13',
  }),
  breadcrumbSchema(crumbs),
  faqSchema(faqItems),
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/blog/maltipoo-daycare-options" schemas={schemas}>
  <article>
    <section class="container-site pt-4">
      <div class="rounded-[var(--radius-panel)] bg-tint-200 px-6 py-10 md:px-12 relative overflow-hidden rise-in">
        <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg class="absolute -top-8 -right-8 w-44 h-44 text-white/40" viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="50" /></svg>
          <svg class="absolute top-6 right-[22%] w-9 h-9 text-primary/25 float-soft" style="--float-rot: 14deg" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="16" cy="19" r="9" /><circle cx="8" cy="11" r="3.4" /><circle cx="16" cy="8.5" r="3.4" /><circle cx="24" cy="11" r="3.4" /></svg>
          <svg class="absolute bottom-5 right-[10%] w-7 h-7 text-primary/20 float-soft" style="--float-rot: -10deg; animation-delay: -2.6s" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="16" cy="19" r="9" /><circle cx="8" cy="11" r="3.4" /><circle cx="16" cy="8.5" r="3.4" /><circle cx="24" cy="11" r="3.4" /></svg>
          <svg class="absolute -bottom-10 -left-10 w-40 h-40 text-primary/8" viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="50" /></svg>
          <div class="absolute bottom-2 left-0 right-0 opacity-30"><PawTrail /></div>
        </div>
        <div class="relative">
        <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} bare class="mb-5" />
        <p class="eyebrow mb-2">Singapore living</p>
        <h1 class="text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.8rem)] mb-3 max-w-[26ch]">Daycare, sitters and helpers for your Maltipoo</h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft m-0">By {site.owners}, AVS licensed pet shop owners · Updated 13 July 2026</p>
      </div></div>
    </section>

    <AnswerCapsule question='What if I cannot be home with my Maltipoo every day?'>
      Build the company from other sources: dog daycare a few days a week, a midday sitter or dog-walker, a helper or grandparent handover, or a split-shift household schedule. A Maltipoo needs presence, not specifically yours; what it cannot do is a silent flat from 8am to 6pm daily.
    </AnswerCapsule>

    <section class="container-site py-6">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-[1.6fr_1fr] gap-8 items-start">
        <div class="pop p-6 md:p-8 text-ink-soft space-y-5 max-w-[72ch]">
          <img data-tilt src={featuredImg.src} width={featuredImg.width} height={featuredImg.height} alt="Maltipoo sitting with a grandmother on a sofa in a multi-generation home" loading="lazy" class="rounded-[var(--radius-media)] w-full h-auto shadow-[var(--shadow-pop)]" />
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">The options menu, honestly ranked</h2>
          <p>
            Best is resident company: a helper, a grandparent, or a household schedule where someone WFHs most days. The dog integrates into a living flat, which is the environment this breed was matched for; the <a href="/blog/maltipoo-with-kids">with-kids guide</a> describes the multi-generation pattern at its best.
          </p>
          <p>
            Next tier is imported company: daycare centres take social dogs for the working day (budget per-day rates and check vaccination requirements), and midday sitters or walkers break the alone-stretch in half. The occasional empty day on top of a trained alone-time foundation is fine; the untrained permanent version is how <a href="/blog/maltipoo-separation-anxiety">separation anxiety</a> is built.
          </p>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">Making a helper handover actually work</h2>
          <p>
            In many Singapore households the helper looks after the dog as its daytime person, and it works beautifully with three ingredients: the helper's genuine willingness (asked, not assumed), inclusion in the training vocabulary so cues stay consistent, and clear ownership of the routine in writing: feeding times, walk timing before the heat, and the toilet protocol.
          </p>
          <p>
            Include the helper in the delivery-day walkthrough and the <a href="/maltipoo-training">free trainer lesson</a>; the person doing the 2pm shift deserves the same briefing as the person paying. The dog, for the record, will adore them; manage your feelings about the favourite-person rankings accordingly.
          </p>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">Daycare due diligence</h2>
          <p>
            Vet the daycare like a preschool: vaccination requirements enforced (a good sign, not friction), toy-dog grouping separate from the big-dog scrum, staff ratios named, and a trial half-day before committing. A 3kg velcro dog in a boisterous free-for-all is not enrichment; a calm small-dog room absolutely is.
          </p>
          <p>
            Start with one or two days a week rather than five; most Maltipoos do best with a mixed week of daycare, home company and the odd trained-alone stretch.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="md:sticky md:top-24">
        <FactsCard
          heading='Daytime company menu'
          items={[
            "Resident: helper, grandparent, WFH split",
            "Imported: daycare days, midday sitter",
            "Foundation: alone-time training regardless",
            "Daycare: toy-dog grouping, trial day first",
            "Silent 8-6 flat daily: not this breed"
          ]}
        />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <FAQ items={faqItems} />

    <CtaClose
      secondaryHeading='Match the routine honestly'
      secondaryText='Tell us your real week on WhatsApp; we will tell you if it works.'
      secondaryHref='/#lifestyle-fit'
      secondaryLabel='Take the routine test'
    />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
